  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Reaction of aniline sulphonic acid with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NaNO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi>COOH</mi></math> gives diazo ester sulphonic acid. Which on further treatment with naphthalene derivative undergoes diazo coupling reaction to give red azo dye.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0012_eac6e0216852.png\" style=\"width: 700px; height: 270px;\"/></p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0012_30864e548e58.png\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 530px;\"/></p><p>This is known as Griess-Ilosvay test. </p>"
